# Line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows; the image and both CI pipelines run on Linux.
# A shell script committed with CRLF fails there as
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which reads like a missing interpreter rather than a line-ending problem and
# costs a full CI cycle to work out. The same applies to the Dockerfile and the
# CI YAML. Pinning these to LF makes it independent of whatever core.autocrlf
# any given clone happens to have.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.task binary
*.ckpt binary
*.pt   binary
